 	<TEXT>
 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_LATE_START_PEDIA</Tag>
 		<English>[H1]Advanced Start[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Advanced Start system allows players to begin a game of Civilization 4 in a later era, customizing their civilization as though they'd played the game up to their starting year. To play an Advanced Start game, go to the "Custom Game" option under the Single Player menu. The Advanced Start checkbox is listed under "Game Options." This option is also available in the multiplayer game setup screen. [BOLD]AdvCiv[\BOLD]: Clarification - Games can be configured to start in a later era without enabling Advanced Start; it's a separate mechanism. About the new Start-Points-as-Handicap option, see the AdvCiv manual. If that option is not selected, then Advanced Start works as described here without fundamental changes.  [NEWLINE][NEWLINE][BOLD]Advanced Start Rules[\BOLD][PARAGRAPH:1]Players will receive a certain amount of Gold which may then be spent on Cities, Buildings, City Population, Culture, Units,  Improvements, Technologies, and Plot Visibility. Certain items, once purchased cannot be removed, so be sure you really want them. These items are: Techs, Cities, Culture, and Visibility. Units and Buildings must be placed in cities. Buildings, Population, and Improvements may all be removed once placed by selecting the item from the Advanced Start menu and then right clicking on the plot where the item you want to remove is located. [PARAGRAPH:1]Leader Traits and Resources which would normally reduce the production time of select buildings or units now provide discounts to such items. For example, an Expansive leader may build [LINK=BUILDING_HARBOR]Harbors[\LINK] at a discount while a leader with access to the Stone resource may build [LINK=BUILDING_WALLS]Walls[\LINK] at half price. The amount of Gold a player receives depends upon the size of the map, the era in which the player begins their game, and their selected Difficulty Level. The later the era, the larger the map, and the lower the selected handicap, the more Gold the player receives. By starting a Custom Game in either Single or Multiplayer, players can adjust the number of Advanced Start points available for that game.[PARAGRAPH:1]The player may then place items on the map. Players may only place items for which they have the appropriate technologies and resources. By using gold to purchase new techs, more advanced units, buildings, etc. become available. Extended visibility may be purchased to expand a player's usable territory. Improvements can give access to necessary resources. Any gold that is not used during the Advanced Start phase is added to the player's treasury when the game starts. </English>
